---
// src/pages/disclaimer.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Legal Disclaimer & Non-Affiliation Declaration"
  description="Official non-government declaration for GovtRecruitments, an independent public recruitment discovery and eligibility platform."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="bg-card rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-12 border border-border shadow-sm">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold bg-blue-50 text-blue-900 border border-blue-200 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
        Statutory Declaration
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-foreground mb-6">
        Legal Disclaimer & Independent Status
      </h1>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-blue-50/80 border border-blue-200 text-blue-950 font-medium">
          <strong>Non-Government Entity:</strong> GovtRecruitments (govtrecruitments.com) is an independently operated educational and career discovery platform. GovtRecruitments is not associated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the Government of India, any state or union-territory government, or any statutory recruitment authority.
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          1. Purpose of the Platform
        </h2>
        <p>
          The sole objective of GovtRecruitments is to assist Indian citizens in understanding and evaluating official government recruitment notifications through deterministic, rule-based algorithms. All eligibility rules, age cutoffs, category relaxations, vacancy breakdowns, and dates are synthesized directly from public gazettes and rulebooks published by official recruitment agencies.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          2. Mandatory User Verification
        </h2>
        <p>
          While GovtRecruitments implements strict 6-stage data verification before publishing any record, recruitment notices remain subject to addenda, corrigenda, postponements, cancellations, or revisions by official authorities at any time. 
          <strong>Users are strictly advised to review the official notification PDF and verify all criteria on official government websites prior to submitting any application form or fee.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          3. Direct Official Portals Directory
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-foreground">
          <li><strong>Central:</strong> <a href="https://www.upsc.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-primary hover:underline">UPSC</a>, <a href="https://ssc.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-primary hover:underline">SSC</a>, and the National Career Service at <a href="https://www.ncs.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-primary hover:underline">ncs.gov.in</a></li>
          <li><strong>States &amp; Union Territories:</strong> the official Public Service Commission, Staff/Subordinate Services Selection Board, Police Recruitment Board, High Court, or department website of the recruiting state (typically a .gov.in or .nic.in domain) named in each notification.</li>
          <li><strong>State application portals and employment exchanges:</strong> each recruitment links to the application portal and registration requirements published by its own state authority.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          4. Zero Financial Transactions
        </h2>
        <p>
          GovtRecruitments does not charge any application fee, registration fee, commission, or brokerage from candidates. We never collect payment card information. All fee payments are conducted strictly on official government portals (such as the relevant state's online portal).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
